      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Maryland Route 26, called Liberty Road, runs through Libertytown and links the town east to Baltimore and southwest to Frederick.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        26,
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Libertytown%2C_Maryland",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "route_only"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Liberty Elementary School opened in 1927, taught grades 1‑12, graduated its last senior class in 1945, and remained a junior high until 1962.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10,
        11,
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Libertytown%2C_Maryland",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Libertytown Park offers picnic gazebos, a rain garden, two baseball fields, a basketball court, three tennis courts, and a large field for football or soccer.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14,
        15,
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Libertytown%2C_Maryland",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "As an unincorporated community, Libertytown has no municipal government and is governed directly by Frederick County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20,
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
